Fail on a read error in read_base64() instead of taking it as EOF.
fgetc() returns EOF for a read error as well as for end of file, and
read_base64() did not check ferror(). base32 -d, base64 -d and uudecode
of base64 data then decoded what they had read so far and exited 0.
Report the error and exit.

---
 libbb/uuencode.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/libbb/uuencode.c
+++ b/libbb/uuencode.c
@@ -238,6 +238,8 @@
 
 		while (!term_seen && in_count < BUFFER_SIZE) {
 			int ch = fgetc(src_stream);
+			if (ch == EOF && ferror(src_stream))
+				bb_simple_perror_msg_and_die(bb_msg_read_error);
 			if (ch == exit_char) {
 				if (in_count == 0)
 					return;
